WEBVTT

00:02.300 --> 00:04.110
A chimera possesses multiple attributes.

00:04.110 --> 00:08.130
Its head is fire, its body is earth, 
and its tail is water.

00:08.470 --> 00:10.810
It'll probably break out of that ice soon.

00:11.490 --> 00:14.980
We can call this the first labor of love 
of our new life together!

00:19.080 --> 00:22.140
Miss Claire, I'll lend you my water magic.

00:22.140 --> 00:24.230
Aim for its fire-based head.

00:24.230 --> 00:28.720
But won't its water-based tail 
still be able to crush us?

00:28.720 --> 00:29.970
Which is why...

00:35.300 --> 00:37.560
The plan will be carried out.

00:38.230 --> 00:39.590
Brother...

00:39.980 --> 00:42.640
It's the only way we can be together.

00:43.650 --> 00:44.920
I get it.

00:44.920 --> 00:47.690
But I'll need some time to build up to that.

00:47.690 --> 00:49.760
I'll buy you the time you need.

00:50.150 --> 00:52.030
You're telling me to trust you?

00:52.990 --> 00:54.240
If you can.

01:06.300 --> 01:08.540
You're worried about Miss Claire, aren't you?

01:08.900 --> 01:11.630
Yes... Well, no, but...

01:20.420 --> 01:23.440
If that made you mad, come get me!

01:26.690 --> 01:29.150
Rae! Where's Miss Claire?!

02:01.310 --> 02:02.780
<i>Okay! This is the spot!</i>

02:05.900 --> 02:07.110
Freeze!

02:09.360 --> 02:11.010
Now, Miss Claire!

02:19.270 --> 02:22.870
Really... You make it sound so simple.

02:24.250 --> 02:26.510
Didn't I tell you before?

02:26.510 --> 02:29.380
This spell is exponentially 
more powerful than my others.

02:31.350 --> 02:33.390
If my hand slips even the slightest bit,

02:33.390 --> 02:35.440
the spell will hit you, too.

02:35.440 --> 02:37.010
I'll be fine.

02:37.010 --> 02:39.140
I know you won't miss.

02:42.840 --> 02:43.770
Light!

02:46.190 --> 02:47.560
Magic Ray!

03:19.860 --> 03:22.610
<i>Even if I can't stay with her...</i>

03:31.230 --> 03:34.820
<i>Miss Claire isn't alone anymore.</i>

05:05.950 --> 05:10.960
<b>Episode 9</b>

05:05.950 --> 05:10.960
<b>My Master Will Never Change</b>

05:11.960 --> 05:13.920
We did it, Miss Claire.

05:15.290 --> 05:17.590
We're lucky it worked out so well.

05:17.590 --> 05:19.390
Really, what a mess.

05:19.390 --> 05:21.180
Truly impressive.

05:22.680 --> 05:24.930
But you're still just a spoiled, rich girl.

05:24.930 --> 05:26.050
Miss Claire!

05:34.190 --> 05:35.660
Prince Thane!

05:36.320 --> 05:37.370
You're bleeding!

05:37.370 --> 05:39.570
I'm fine. He only grazed me.

05:39.570 --> 05:41.570
Well, well!

05:43.830 --> 05:45.870
If it isn't the failure of a prince!

05:46.220 --> 05:49.370
Who are you? 
Were you the one behind all this?

05:52.550 --> 05:56.400
My original goal was to kill 
as many nobles as possible,

05:56.400 --> 05:58.420
but this is more than I'd hoped for.

06:00.100 --> 06:01.890
Have a good taste of it.

06:03.500 --> 06:04.410
He got away!

06:04.410 --> 06:05.890
Prince Thane!

06:05.890 --> 06:08.040
Prince Thane! Prince Thane!

06:08.040 --> 06:08.890
This is...

06:23.070 --> 06:25.310
Don't die, Prince Thane!

06:25.740 --> 06:29.170
Stay back, Miss Claire. 
It's a new type of poison.

06:29.170 --> 06:30.200
I'll neutralize it.

06:55.440 --> 06:57.150
He'll be all right now.

06:57.690 --> 06:59.290
You saved him?

06:59.290 --> 07:00.210
Yes.

07:02.620 --> 07:03.940
Thank goodness...

07:07.520 --> 07:10.830
That was cantarella, a deadly poison 
from the Nur Empire.

07:12.070 --> 07:14.720
Then that man was from the Nur Empire?

07:14.720 --> 07:15.960
Most likely.

07:15.960 --> 07:18.830
<b>Bauer Kingdom</b>

07:15.960 --> 07:18.830
<b>Nur Empire</b>

07:15.960 --> 07:18.830
<b>Nur Empire</b>

07:15.960 --> 07:18.830
<b>Sousse Kingdom</b>

07:16.490 --> 07:19.480
<i>Whenever a major incident 
occurs in this world,</i>

07:19.480 --> 07:22.340
<i>the Nur Empire, an enemy nation, 
is always involved.</i>

07:22.750 --> 07:25.540
<i>There's an event in 
the latter half of the game</i>

07:25.540 --> 07:28.970
<i>where they use cantarella and the heroine 
has to come up with an antidote.</i>

07:29.380 --> 07:32.090
<i>Things worked out because I knew that, but...</i>

07:32.090 --> 07:33.720
Rae! Claire!

07:34.850 --> 07:35.870
Thane?!

07:35.870 --> 07:37.860
Hey! What the hell happened?!

07:37.860 --> 07:39.700
The enemy poisoned him.

07:40.560 --> 07:44.340
I neutralized the poison, 
but take him to a doctor just in case.

07:45.220 --> 07:46.320
I swear...

07:47.460 --> 07:49.320
He just had to charge in alone.

07:50.400 --> 07:52.200
That idiot.

07:55.890 --> 07:57.960
The Aurousseau duo are in custody.

08:06.750 --> 08:07.970
Lene...

08:15.170 --> 08:19.180
<i>The incident was brought 
to an end very quickly.</i>

08:23.840 --> 08:27.490
The protesters are gone, and the 
Commoner Movement has fallen quiet.

08:27.890 --> 08:30.660
Well, we learned Dede 
had been falsely accused,

08:30.660 --> 08:33.330
and that the Nur Empire 
was behind everything.

08:33.670 --> 08:37.710
I can't believe we were playing right 
into the enemy nation's hands.

08:39.460 --> 08:41.960
Will the Aurousseau family be ruined?

08:41.960 --> 08:43.440
Probably.

08:43.440 --> 08:47.060
Even if they were being manipulated, 
what's done is done.

08:47.060 --> 08:50.120
They've already been removed from 
all business involving magic stones,

08:50.120 --> 08:52.900
and they're now awaiting 
the kingdom's ruling.

08:52.900 --> 08:55.220
And what about Lene and Lambert?

08:59.060 --> 09:02.980
<i>What Master Lambert and Lene did 
amounts to treason against the kingdom.</i>

09:03.520 --> 09:05.590
<i>The death penalty is unavoidable.</i>

09:06.110 --> 09:08.360
Oh, yeah! Claire, Rae...

09:09.380 --> 09:12.390
Apparently, you two are getting a reward.

09:12.390 --> 09:14.320
A... reward?

09:14.320 --> 09:16.260
You're the ones who identified 
the real mastermind

09:16.260 --> 09:19.480
and shattered the enemy 
nation's plans, after all.

09:19.480 --> 09:21.980
And Rae saved Thane's life, to boot.

09:21.980 --> 09:24.820
I'd say you'll be summoned 
to the royal palace pretty soon.

09:24.820 --> 09:27.590
Father wants to bestow your rewards in person.

09:27.590 --> 09:30.050
But I didn't do anything so—

09:30.380 --> 09:34.420
Wow, is that so? We'll gratefully 
accept whatever he offers!

09:34.420 --> 09:35.700
Right, Miss Claire?

09:35.700 --> 09:37.470
What do you think you're doing?!

09:37.470 --> 09:39.140
Listen to me, Miss Claire!

09:39.140 --> 09:42.880
Whisper, whisper, whisper...

09:43.760 --> 09:46.940
I see. Well, it's worth a try.

10:02.760 --> 10:05.920
Can't you relax? Just sit down and wait.

10:05.920 --> 10:09.050
Well, I don't want my outfit to wrinkle...

10:09.590 --> 10:14.210
Miss Claire! Thank you for preparing 
such a fine outfit for me!

10:14.210 --> 10:17.300
It's not as if I did it for you.

10:17.300 --> 10:20.650
I would be the one humiliated 
if you turned up looking like a slob.

10:20.650 --> 10:24.250
Oh, there you go again! 
I know you did it out of love!

10:24.250 --> 10:25.440
Shut up.

10:26.900 --> 10:27.810
Honestly...

10:28.390 --> 10:30.780
You'd actually look the part 
if you kept quiet.

10:30.780 --> 10:31.530
Huh?

10:31.860 --> 10:33.450
I didn't say anything.

10:35.280 --> 10:38.200
Claire François. Rae Taylor.

10:38.200 --> 10:40.790
You are granted an audience 
with His Royal Majesty.

10:57.560 --> 10:59.330
Lift your heads.

11:05.190 --> 11:08.510
I have heard that you brought 
the recent series of incidents

11:05.230 --> 11:09.900
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

11:05.230 --> 11:09.900
<b>King l'Ausseil Bauer</b>

11:08.510 --> 11:11.260
at the Royal Academy to a conclusion,

11:10.690 --> 11:14.570
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

11:10.690 --> 11:14.570
<b>Queen Riche Bauer</b>

11:11.260 --> 11:14.570
and that it was you 
who saved Thane's life, as well.

11:15.150 --> 11:16.630
These are great deeds.

11:17.010 --> 11:20.350
I will grant you an extra-special reward.

11:20.350 --> 11:22.390
Tell me what you desire.

11:25.750 --> 11:31.450
I sincerely thank you for 
granting us this audience today.

11:31.450 --> 11:33.460
<i>I'm counting on you, Miss Claire.</i>

11:33.790 --> 11:39.470
<i>As a commoner, I'm not allowed 
to speak directly to the king.</i>

11:39.470 --> 11:43.850
With regards to our reward, there is 
one thing I wish to ask of you.

11:44.140 --> 11:45.760
Let us hear it.

11:45.760 --> 11:46.690
At once.

11:47.980 --> 11:49.840
<i>This is it. The moment of truth.</i>

11:51.520 --> 11:55.530
I petition you to spare 
the lives of the Aurousseaus.

12:05.150 --> 12:09.670
I have been told that the Aurousseaus were 
the principal offenders in this incident.

12:10.110 --> 12:14.030
Are you telling me that you seek 
a commutation of their sentence?

12:14.030 --> 12:19.590
Yes. I request that you grant them a pardon.

12:21.410 --> 12:23.600
Salas, what do you think?

12:24.540 --> 12:26.190
That will be difficult.

12:26.190 --> 12:28.980
To reward meritorious deeds and punish crime 
is the fundamental rule of law.

12:29.370 --> 12:32.500
There is no reason to commute 
the Aurousseaus' sentence.

12:33.740 --> 12:35.370
<i>I guess it won't work...</i>

12:35.780 --> 12:39.610
The Aurousseau family has always 
devoted itself to its kingdom.

12:39.610 --> 12:42.980
With regard to the business 
of magic stones, in particular,

12:42.980 --> 12:45.760
their contributions are by no means trivial.

12:46.430 --> 12:50.120
Please consider making 
an exception to pardon them.

12:53.000 --> 12:54.420
That is true.

12:54.420 --> 12:58.760
Is it infeasible to commute their sentence 
in light of their contributions, Salas?

12:58.760 --> 13:01.980
Their crimes are too great 
to be offset by their works.

13:02.420 --> 13:05.890
Inviting a foreign threat and the attempted 
murder of royalty and nobility

13:05.890 --> 13:07.670
are unforgivable crimes.

13:08.140 --> 13:11.020
They are unlikely to receive 
anything short of execution.

13:12.540 --> 13:16.020
So it shall be. Speak a different wish.

13:19.960 --> 13:25.200
Your Majesty, would you please 
consider granting their request?

13:29.460 --> 13:30.920
Thane?

13:36.750 --> 13:41.220
This strife was caused by 
dissatisfaction toward the nobility.

13:41.220 --> 13:44.680
And the sentiment that 
triggered this insurrection

13:44.680 --> 13:48.130
was the belief that an injustice 
was committed in favor of nobles.

13:49.640 --> 13:53.440
If you fail to show the people that 
you do not look down upon commoners,

13:53.800 --> 13:55.870
the same thing will likely happen again.

13:56.590 --> 14:00.690
And you believe that sparing 
the Aurousseaus will help the matter?

14:01.040 --> 14:01.950
I do.

14:01.950 --> 14:04.450
With all due respect, 
Your Majesty, Prince Thane...

14:05.260 --> 14:07.640
There is suspicion that 
the Aurousseaus were the ones

14:07.640 --> 14:10.530
who instigated the Commoner Movement.

14:10.530 --> 14:15.080
If you spare them, the nobles whose children 
were endangered will not stand for it.

14:15.080 --> 14:18.020
In terms of the importance of magic,

14:18.020 --> 14:20.830
it is clear that great value must 
be placed not only upon nobles,

14:20.830 --> 14:23.890
but also upon commoners, 
who are greater in number.

14:23.890 --> 14:27.190
If you do not wish to let your policy 
of meritocracy become empty words,

14:27.190 --> 14:28.470
please reconsider.

14:30.170 --> 14:32.850
I have heard what both sides have to say.

14:38.060 --> 14:41.360
The Aurousseau family will be 
exiled from this kingdom.

14:43.700 --> 14:45.500
Your Majesty! With all due respect—

14:45.500 --> 14:47.300
I will brook no argument.

14:47.940 --> 14:48.940
Yes, sire.

14:49.900 --> 14:53.460
The details of their exile 
will be imparted at a later date.

14:53.830 --> 14:58.010
Claire François, Rae Taylor, you may go.

15:07.980 --> 15:09.950
We did it!

15:07.980 --> 15:09.950
We did it!

15:11.220 --> 15:12.710
Don't copy me.

15:13.140 --> 15:15.070
That was our minds working as one!

15:15.070 --> 15:18.350
Come on, just let yourself 
be happy, Miss Claire!

15:18.350 --> 15:21.110
I don't see why I need to share joy with you!

15:21.110 --> 15:22.280
Then let's share love instead!

15:22.280 --> 15:23.740
What are you even talking about?!

15:24.040 --> 15:27.240
We did it! We did it! We really did it!

15:27.240 --> 15:30.230
We did it! We did it!

15:30.450 --> 15:32.490
Miss Claire!

15:52.300 --> 15:53.380
Miss Claire.

15:55.220 --> 15:57.960
<i>All of the Aurousseaus' assets were seized,</i>

15:57.960 --> 16:00.610
<i>and they were exiled to a neighboring country.</i>

16:01.500 --> 16:05.390
Do you think the Aurousseaus 
will get along okay in the Alpes?

16:05.390 --> 16:08.290
I've heard the head of the family, 
Bartley, is quite competent.

16:08.780 --> 16:11.780
I'm sure they'll earn enough to 
keep food on the table, at least.

16:12.480 --> 16:16.370
I heard they're disowning 
Lene and Master Lambert.

16:17.440 --> 16:18.600
Even so...

16:18.920 --> 16:22.090
As long as they're alive, 
things will work out.

16:30.860 --> 16:31.950
Lene!

16:47.470 --> 16:49.360
Rae, Miss Claire...

16:49.850 --> 16:52.300
Miss Claire said she wanted to say goodbye.

16:52.300 --> 16:56.340
Y-You're the one who threw a tantrum 
insisting that I bring you here!

16:56.340 --> 16:58.700
Where you are, there I shall be, as well.

16:58.700 --> 17:01.720
I'll be with you wherever you go. Don't worry!

17:01.720 --> 17:03.500
I absolutely will worry!

17:06.250 --> 17:08.480
I'm sorry. I couldn't help it.

17:08.480 --> 17:10.510
You're just acting the same as always.

17:15.200 --> 17:17.270
Lene, I...

17:23.280 --> 17:25.290
They could have executed my brother and I,

17:25.290 --> 17:29.000
along with the rest of our family, 
and none would have batted an eye.

17:29.000 --> 17:33.580
We're only here as we are now 
because of you two.

17:34.310 --> 17:38.450
Thank you for stopping us.

17:44.320 --> 17:45.570
I'm sorry.

17:52.030 --> 17:52.750
Miss Claire—

17:52.750 --> 17:54.140
Time's up.

17:54.140 --> 17:56.010
Lene, here.

18:00.890 --> 18:04.400
They're new recipes. 
Use mayonnaise where you're going, too.

18:04.400 --> 18:05.680
I can?

18:05.680 --> 18:09.650
Yeah. It should help you 
make some money, at least.

18:12.020 --> 18:13.530
Thank you.

18:15.850 --> 18:18.960
Well, Rae, Miss Claire...

18:19.510 --> 18:21.130
Thank you for everything.

18:22.060 --> 18:23.900
Goodbye, Lene.

18:36.240 --> 18:38.510
Miss Claire, don't you want to say anything?

18:53.460 --> 18:54.900
Lene!

18:56.760 --> 18:58.740
I won't say goodbye!

18:59.430 --> 19:01.620
Stay healthy, wherever you are,

19:02.050 --> 19:04.620
and we'll meet again someday!

19:10.880 --> 19:13.830
I told you, I don't care what your name is!

19:13.830 --> 19:16.010
What I want you to do 
right now is be a horse!

19:17.010 --> 19:19.390
You are my servant—

19:19.390 --> 19:21.640
the servant of Claire François.

19:21.640 --> 19:24.270
That makes you the highest-ranked 
commoner in this kingdom!

19:24.270 --> 19:25.890
Take pride in that!

19:28.900 --> 19:30.590
Lene! Lene!

19:30.590 --> 19:33.740
I met the princes!

19:33.740 --> 19:35.110
Lene!

19:35.110 --> 19:36.490
Lene.

19:36.840 --> 19:38.190
Lene...

19:39.790 --> 19:40.790
Lene...

19:54.240 --> 19:56.230
She was a good master for you.

19:57.240 --> 19:59.650
Not "was."

20:01.160 --> 20:02.560
Miss Claire...

20:04.480 --> 20:06.990
will be my master always and forever.

20:16.380 --> 20:18.120
Well, they're gone.

20:19.670 --> 20:20.880
Miss Claire...

20:21.500 --> 20:22.700
What is it?

20:23.120 --> 20:24.620
May I hug you?

20:26.950 --> 20:29.930
Of course not. Let's go.

20:37.010 --> 20:39.730
Wh-What are you doing?!

20:39.990 --> 20:42.500
Get off of me!

20:42.500 --> 20:44.010
It's okay to cry.

20:44.680 --> 20:45.980
Don't be ridiculous!

20:45.980 --> 20:49.490
Why should losing a single maid make me—

20:50.100 --> 20:54.610
It's okay. I can't see your face
when I'm holding you like this.

20:54.610 --> 20:56.690
I told you... I...

20:56.690 --> 20:58.990
You don't want to say goodbye 
to Lene, do you?

21:11.390 --> 21:14.810
This world really isn't fair, is it?

21:15.430 --> 21:18.260
We can't even love the one we want to.

21:30.330 --> 21:33.400
You are incredibly audacious 
for a commoner, you know that?

21:33.700 --> 21:36.880
Yes! So please punish me for it!

21:37.780 --> 21:41.650
Absolutely not. You would 
consider it a reward.

21:43.350 --> 21:46.690
You finally understand me, Miss Claire!

21:46.690 --> 21:48.540
All that's left is for us to get married!

21:48.540 --> 21:50.040
That is not happening!

21:50.860 --> 21:54.060
Aw, Miss Claire!

21:59.030 --> 22:00.770
I hope we see her again.

22:01.240 --> 22:03.370
We will. I'm sure of it.

23:46.730 --> 23:49.200
Hey, did you hear? <i>She's</i> coming.

23:49.200 --> 23:52.080
Yes, and it was decided quite suddenly.

23:52.080 --> 23:55.740
It's perfect timing, though. 
Claire seems pretty down.

23:55.740 --> 23:57.330
Huh? What do you mean?

23:57.330 --> 24:00.530
Well, she was Claire's first love, wasn't she?

23:59.540 --> 24:01.040
<b>Episode 10</b>

23:59.540 --> 24:01.040
<b>My New Rival in Love Is a Perfect Superhuman</b>
